course: dictionary
lesson: 9462
title: Starling: a bird and a word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A starling is a common bird with dark, shiny feathers. In the sun they look purple and green, and in winter they are covered in small pale spots. Starling is a noun, so you can say a starling or some starlings.
explain: The word can also name a group. «Tens of thousands of starlings fly together before roosting in shapes called murmurations.» The context tells you a murmuration is a big flock that moves together in shapes. Read the words around a new word to find its meaning.
explain: Context also shows what starlings do. «Starlings copy other birds, phones, car alarms and even human words.» Copy is the clue: a starling can sound like a phone ringing. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence and asking whether it still makes sense.
fact: A starling is a common bird with dark, shiny feathers that look purple and green in the sun.
fact: A large swirling flock of starlings in the evening sky is called a murmuration.
fact: Each bird in a murmuration watches about 7 of its nearest neighbours.
fact: Starlings are clever mimics and can copy car alarms and phone ringtones.
fact: Starlings live in Europe, and were brought to North America, Australia and New Zealand, where they are now very common.
exercise: «Starlings swirl over the roofs at dusk.» What does dusk mean? | The early morning before sunrise | The middle of the day | *The time in the evening when the light fades | The middle of winter
exercise: «Tens of thousands of starlings fly together before roosting in shapes called murmurations.» What is a murmuration? | *A large swirling flock of starlings in the evening sky | A kind of bird food | A single starling sitting on a fence | A bird with bright red feathers
exercise: «Starlings copy other birds, phones, car alarms and even human words.» Find and copy one word that means to do the same as something else. | birds | alarms | *copy | phones
test: «Microraptor had feathers that were shiny black like a starling's.» What colour do a starling's feathers look in the sun? | Bright red and gold | Pale grey all year | *Purple and green | Blue and white
test: «Starlings are clever mimics.» What does mimic mean? | A bird that sings only at night | A person who tells jokes | *Something that copies sounds or actions | A nest built in a tree
exam: «A falcon finds it hard to pick one bird out.» What does this show about starlings in a murmuration? | Starlings never fly in the sky | *Starlings fly so close together that one is hard to spot | Starlings are slow and easy to catch | Starlings are sleeping in the trees
